      "writtenOn": "2019-06-06T22:57:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I tried to cast the supertype to a subtype. Thanks for your detailed explanation.\n\nI agree that if we do not touch the stack we can not do the static type checking all the way. In your suggestion of passing in an array, if I understand correctly, this array contains the state entry chain and is used to replace the stack right ? If we do not do the stack refactoring soon can I just leave it  \"(State\u003c? super T\u003e) (mStateStack[i].state))\" for now ?",
      "parentUuid": "5830f5e6_d2fd9f44",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1073,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 1073,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "a283c12512af5783ff7876d2ef76a681e886ea55",
